    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 3 USER]\ne021\tI am not sure disclaimers solve it.\ne022\tResearchers often ignore “beta” once they have invested in a workflow.\ne023\tIf we change the data model later, they may feel we broke something even if we warned them.\ne024\tAlso, the two labs want to cite the tool in papers this year.\ne025\tA public version would make that easier and may help our grant renewal, but I do not want citation pressure to freeze an interface we chose for convenience.\n[Turn 3 ASSISTANT]\ne026\tThen the most consequential commitment may be the data and output format, not the release label.\ne027\tYou could mark some interfaces as experimental while stabilizing a minimal exchange format for saved projects.\ne028\tBut that creates engineering work and may imply more compatibility than you can guarantee.\ne029\tThe publication and grant benefits are real organizational incentives; they should be named openly rather than translated into an argument that users necessarily need the current interface now.",
