    "prior_context": {
      "alternative_citation_allowed": false,
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 2 USER]\ne011\tThat is close to what the maintainers say, but the structured preview has been “one more cohort” for six months.\ne012\tEach time we add users, we find another thing to document before going public.\ne013\tMeanwhile two volunteer contributors have stopped attending meetings because there is no visible release.\ne014\tI do not think contributor momentum is superficial.\ne015\tA tool that is always almost ready can become a private service for our friends.\n[Turn 2 ASSISTANT]\ne016\tAgreed—indefinite preview is itself a product choice, and it can narrow both the community and the evidence you receive.\ne017\tA public beta can create a focal point for contributors if its limits are explicit.\ne018\tThe maintainers' concern still matters because public access changes the volume and variety of support.\ne019\tThe question may be less “is it ready?”\ne020\tthan “what support promise accompanies the release, and can the team sustain that promise?”",
